WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.379
INTRO:
Usually, car salesmen are thought to be the

00:00:02.379 --> 00:00:07.839
slimiest and most manipulative people in the
world. Aside from using pushy sales tactics

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:13.040
and predatory financing, car salesmen often
don’t mind selling you a piece of trash.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.710
In fact, they’ll probably do it with a smile.
Considering this, I don’t think you’d

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:21.970
be surprised to hear that 87% of American
adults dislike something about the car buying

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.439
process. Also, if you’re one of the few
people who had a positive experience, many

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:31.419
would argue that you got taken advantage of
so much that you didn’t even realize. But,

00:00:31.419 --> 00:00:36.490
one guy named Bob Brockman actually took advantage
of car dealerships so hard that they didn’t

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:41.090
even realize. Throughout his career, Bob sold
overpriced software and hardware to dealerships

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:45.690
across the nation, often with multi-decade
long contracts. And after he was done milking

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.120
the dealerships, Bob turned around and tried
to milk the government. But this didn’t

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.530
work out too well as he was charged with the
largest tax evasion charge in history. So,

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.200
here’s how Bob Brockman made billions by
taking advantage of dealerships and the government,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.090
and how he eventually got caught.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:07.260
BOB BROCKMAN:
Taking a look back, Bob Brockman was born

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:13.400
in 1941 in St. Petersburg, Florida. This was
just before the US joined World War 2, so

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:17.820
Bob was born at the height of the war. But,
this wasn’t too bad for Bob as the war would

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:23.110
come to an end by the time he turned 5. Anyway,
his dad owned a gas station and his mom worked

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:28.290
as a physiotherapist, so he had a pretty comfortable
life financially. This allowed him to focus

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:33.159
on his education and excel in school. In fact,
he graduated summa cum laude, which is the

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:38.200
highest distinction, from the University of
Florida with a business degree in 1963. Bob

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.310
was also a member of the university’s business
honor society, so there’s no doubt that

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:46.770
he was a pretty sharp guy. Out of college,
Bob got a marketing job at a Ford while also

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:51.350
serving in the US Marine Reserves. This didn’t
last long though as Bob switched over to IBM

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:56.340
in 1966, and this is where he really got his
foundation for selling. Bob was tasked with

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:01.119
the job of selling IBM’s mainframe computer
services to car dealers. And out of the gate,

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:06.150
Bob was a star performer. Maybe it was his
young ambition or his time at Ford, we’ll

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:11.030
probably never know, but it seemed like Bob
was born to sell. Being the star that he was,

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:16.900
Bob knew that he didn’t really need IBM,
so in 1970, he left the company and launched

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.590
his own company called Universal Computer
Services. During his time at IBM, Bob had

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:26.350
dealt with dozens of car dealerships, and
he knew exactly what they wanted: less paperwork.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:30.340
So, he taught himself how to code and developed
a piece of software that could synthesize

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:34.760
multiple financial statements into one. For
people who owned multiple car dealerships,

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:39.010
this was a godsend. Soon enough, Bob expanded
his software to help dealers with managing

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:43.560
inventory, generating weekly reports, and
tracking sales, and car dealerships ate this

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.701
up. Bob leaned into this business over the
next 20 years and he got quite rich as in

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:51.840
he made hundreds of millions. Up until this
point, Bob hadn’t really done anything slimy

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.550
per se. Sure, he might’ve used some shady
sales tactics when selling to dealerships,

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:01.060
but for the most part, Bob was simply offering
an extremely valuable service to dealers,

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:04.819
and he was rewarded quite handsomely. His
next business move, however, wasn’t nearly

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:05.819
as moral.

00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:12.290
MASQUERADING AS FORD:
In the early 1990s, Ford decided that they

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.740
were done with the IT world, so they started
looking for buyers for their IT division.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:21.380
Given that this was right up Bob’s alley,
he made an offer for $103 million, but he

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:26.840
had one condition. He wanted the rights to
use Ford’s logos and branding for 5 years.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:31.769
Now, this was a pretty odd request, but Bob
was already running a respectable software

00:03:31.769 --> 00:03:36.200
business, and Ford probably thought that Bob
simply wanted some time to rebrand the company.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:41.940
So, they agreed to the deal, but this turned
out to be a big mistake. You see, Bob leveraged

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.540
the trust and respect dealers had for Ford
in order to sneak in extremely predatory deals.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:51.810
He charged ludicrous amounts for everyday
tech. This included charges such as a $12,000

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:56.350
fee to install a 500-megabyte hard drive or
a $2400 for a printer. You would think that

00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:00.280
dealers would’ve caught onto these ridiculous
fees, but many of them didn’t look into

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:05.069
the fine print and simply trusted Ford because
the fine print was a 12-inch thick contract.

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:09.000
When Bob’s 5-year license for Ford’s branding
was up though, many of these dealers were

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.159
in for a rude awakening. Some of them tried
to rebel against Bob alleging that he had

00:04:13.159 --> 00:04:18.019
misled them, but Bob was well prepared for
this. Any complaint from the dealers was already

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:21.770
accounted for in the fine print, and dealers
couldn’t just wait it out given that these

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:26.380
contracts often extended decades. So, many
of them tried to go the litigation route by

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:31.430
suing Bob. But this just drowned them in legal
fees which were often just as bad as Bob's

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:36.500
fees. At the time, it wasn’t really clear
how bad these dealerships were getting screwed.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.900
Dealers that weren’t affected simply dismissed
the concerns as they should’ve read the

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:44.660
fine print. It wasn’t until 10 to 15 years
later that Bob’s damages finally came to

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:49.630
light as these dealerships began to file for
bankruptcy and shut down due to his fees.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:54.650
In 2010, for example, a Californian entrepreneur
named Jay Gill decided to expand his empire

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:58.770
by purchasing a group of 10 car dealerships.
But, when he looked into the financials of

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:02.900
the group, he realized that the company owed
Bob $3 million and that they were supposed

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:09.250
to pay him $35,000 every single month. After
seeing this, Jay said quote, “I know unequivocally

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.900
that I wouldn’t do business with this guy,
even if it was free.” Fortunately for Jay,

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:17.960
he didn’t have to deal with Bob for that
long as he agreed to settle half that amount,

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:22.710
but with fees like that, it’s no wonder
why car salesmen are so pushy. If they don’t

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:27.120
rip you off, they can’t afford to get ripped
off themselves.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.220
DOCUPAD:
As you would guess, the entire fiasco with

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:35.340
Ford wasn’t the best for Universal Computer
Service’s public reputation. So, Bob started

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:40.040
looking to rebrand himself in the 2000s, and
the perfect opportunity came in 2006 when

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:44.370
he got the opportunity to sell his company
to Reynolds and Reynolds. Similar to UCS,

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:48.490
Reynolds and Reynolds had been selling software
to auto dealers since the 1980s. They had

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:52.010
mostly grown their software empire through
a bunch of acquisitions and offering to buy

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:56.150
UCS was just another one of their routine
acquisitions. I don’t think they did much

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:00.640
due diligence as a simple glance at Bob’s
history would probably off-put most people.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:05.740
Nevertheless, Reynolds and Reynolds went ahead
and purchased UCS for $2.8 billion, and as

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:10.490
you would guess, in Brockman fashion, there
was a critical contingency for the acquisition.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.260
Bob stipulated that he must be made CEO of
the merged company for the acquisition to

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:18.729
be completed. Reynolds agreed and it didn’t
take long for Bob to start ruining Reynolds’

00:06:18.729 --> 00:06:22.830
reputation either. First of all, he went ahead
and implemented some smaller rules that were

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:27.860
annoying but not too bad. He refused to hire
smokers and forced all employees to get an

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:32.020
annual physical to maintain health insurance.
Some of his other policies, however, were

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:36.270
much more damaging. About ⅓ of Reynolds’
revenue was from General Motors through their

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:40.870
Integrated Dealership Management program.
Considering how integral GM was to the business,

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:45.770
you would think that Bob would treat them
very well. But, in 2007, GM ended up filing

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:49.860
a lawsuit against Reynolds accusing them of
refusing to make requested changes to the

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:55.240
software. Reynolds ended up settling with
GM a year later which ended the GM partnership.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:07:00.050
Somehow, Reynolds had already lost their biggest
customer just two years after Bob took over,

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:05.470
but Bob didn’t care as he had his eye on
a much bigger prize. In 2007, a company called

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:10.740
Coindata came out with a product called DocuPAD.
DocuPAD is basically a large tabletop tablet

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.490
that eliminates the need for paperwork when
selling a car. This makes it much easier for

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:19.250
car salesmen to upsell customers on insurance
programs and amenities that they simply don’t

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:23.600
need. Despite the appealing product, most
car dealerships avoided the system given that

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:28.920
it was extremely expensive. Coindata charged
$10,000 to set up each system and then an

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:33.639
additional $1000 every month as a maintenance
fee. And if the dealership wanted to modify

00:07:33.639 --> 00:07:38.770
anything, they were charged an extra $297
for each modification. Coindata had a tough

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:42.900
time getting dealerships to pick up these
tabs, but Bob wasn’t worried about that.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:48.160
In 2009, he offered to form an exclusive marketing
partnership with Coindata, and over the next

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:53.710
two years, they revamped the system. In 2011,
the duo came out with a new DocuPAD, and with

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:58.160
Bob at the wheel, these sold like hotcakes.
It’s still not clear if these systems are

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:02.470
actually worth it for dealerships, but there
was no question that they were worth it for

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:03.720
Bob.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:08.870
TAX EVASION:
By this point, Bob was raking in billions,

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:13.240
and though his business could be labeled as
immoral or unethical, it definitely wasn’t

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:18.229
illegal. It would’ve been in Bob’s best
interest to keep it this way, but unfortunately,

00:08:18.229 --> 00:08:22.410
it didn’t take long for greed to get to
him. In the late 1990s, an investment banker

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:27.090
from Goldman Sachs named Robert F. Smith reached
out to Bob. Originally, he offered to buy

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:31.729
out UCS from Bob, but Bob turned the script
on Robert. Bob offered to help Robert start

00:08:31.729 --> 00:08:36.729
up a new investment bank called Vista Equity
Partners with $1 billion. But, in return,

00:08:36.729 --> 00:08:41.909
Bob wanted Robert to help him set up a foreign
trust that didn’t report to the IRS. Technically,

00:08:41.909 --> 00:08:46.089
there were legal ways to accomplish this and
legitimate reasons to do so, but I think it

00:08:46.089 --> 00:08:50.430
was pretty clear that Bob was going to use
this for illegal purposes. Nonetheless, this

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:55.379
was an opportunity of a lifetime for Robert,
so he took Bob up on this offer. The Department

00:08:55.379 --> 00:08:59.970
Of Justice has since labeled this deal as
evidence of conspiracy and scheme and artifice

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:04.480
to defraud. So, here’s how the fraud worked.
Bob owned a charitable trust called Eugene

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:09.019
Brockman that was based in Bermuda. This charitable
trust owned a holding company called Spanish

00:09:09.019 --> 00:09:13.480
Steps Holdings registered in Nevis. And Spanish
Steps Holdings owned a company called Point

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:17.589
Investments which was registered in the British
Virgin Islands. And Point Investments was

00:09:17.589 --> 00:09:22.019
investing in Vista’s foreign fund. Bob used
this convoluted string of companies to funnel

00:09:22.019 --> 00:09:27.420
money offshore and avoid taxes. Bob and Robert
got away with this for decades, but eventually,

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:32.470
the IRS caught on. Robert didn’t resist
the IRS much and quickly turned on Bob. When

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:36.839
he took in the investment from Bob, he knew
this could eventually happen, and he was prepared

00:09:36.839 --> 00:09:40.929
for it. Robert worked with the IRS to give
them all the information they needed, and

00:09:40.929 --> 00:09:45.899
he happily paid the $139 million fine for
his involvement in the scheme. From his perspective,

00:09:45.899 --> 00:09:50.320
the deal with Bob was well worth it. Vista
Equity Partners had grown to $86 billion in

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:55.879
assets under management which made Robert
worth $8.9 billion. Considering this, a $139

00:09:55.879 --> 00:10:00.670
million fee wasn’t that bad. As for Bob,
his lawyers tried to argue that he was suffering

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:04.579
from dementia and that he couldn’t serve
jail time, but courts dismissed this argument

00:10:04.579 --> 00:10:08.639
in November. We still don’t know what the
final sentence is going to be, but it’s

00:10:08.639 --> 00:10:12.800
probably not going to be that forgiving. At
this point though, it doesn’t really matter

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:17.540
that much. Bob is already 80 years old, so
he’s already avoided paying for his crimes

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:21.850
for most of his life. Aside from this, the
latest accounts suggest that Bob is worth

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:26.949
$4.7 billion. So, even if he was charged a
multi-hundred million dollar fine or even

00:10:26.949 --> 00:10:31.410
a billion-dollar fine, it wouldn't actually
hurt him that much financially. Really, the

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:34.959
worst punishment he could get at this point
is being forced to live out his last days

00:10:34.959 --> 00:10:40.200
in jail, and that might very well end up happening,
but we’ll just have to wait and see. What

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:44.910
do you guys think should be Bob’s punishment?
Comment that down below. Also, drop a like

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:49.249
if you’re glad that Bob gave car dealers
a taste of their own medicine. And of course,

00:10:49.249 --> 00:10:52.749
consider checking out our international channels
